<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <title><%= content_for(:title) || 'Comrade' %></title>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1,interactive-widget=resizes-content">
    <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
    <meta name="application-name" content="Comrade">
    <meta name="mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
    <%= csrf_meta_tags %>
    <%= csp_meta_tag %>

    <%= yield :head %>

    <link rel="icon" href="/icon.png" type="image/png">
    <link rel="icon" href="/icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/icon.png">
    <%# The OpenSearch handoff: visiting the app lets Firefox offer
        "Add Comrade" from the address bar's magnifier, putting the
        whole ask behind one GET to /search. %>
    <%= tag.link rel: 'search', type: 'application/opensearchdescription+xml', title: 'Comrade', href: opensearch_path %>

    <%# The Ledger's three voices: Oswald for the poster, Source Serif 4
        for everything a reader reads, JetBrains Mono for the press's
        small furniture. %>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Oswald:wght@400;500;600&family=Source+Serif+4:ital,opsz,wght@0,8..60,400;0,8..60,600;1,8..60,400&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">

    <%# Restores the saved root font size before first paint (see font_scale_boot.js and the font-sizer controller). %>
    <%= javascript_include_tag 'font_scale_boot' %>
    <%= javascript_include_tag 'visual_viewport_boot' %>
    <%= stylesheet_link_tag :tailwind, "data-turbo-track": 'reload' %>
    <%= javascript_importmap_tags %>
  </head>

  <%# App shell: fixed inset frame — the document never scrolls, so none of
      the iOS viewport-unit states (URL bar × keyboard × accessory) can
      produce dead scroll, pan-on-focus, or scroll carry across the
      post-first-reply Turbo.visit. The transcript panel scrolls internally.
      The masthead opens every page: the poster band, then the sub-band
      whose bottom edge is the Scotch rule. The rail (recents + identity)
      is the desk's third column; the drawer behavior survives on narrow
      viewports, flipped to slide from the right. The gate hides the rail
      and the ☰ until the reader chooses — "stay in the commune" reveals
      them client-side along with the composer. %>
  <% gated = current_enlistee.blank? && request.path.in?([root_path, conversations_path]) %>
  <% edition_word = Time.current.hour < 12 ? 'morning edition' : Time.current.hour < 18 ? 'afternoon edition' : 'evening edition' %>
  <body class="c-beyond font-serif text-newsprint-dim antialiased overflow-hidden" data-controller="sidebar-drawer lightbox" data-action="keydown->lightbox#keydown">
    <%# Narrow viewports: the ☰ summons the rail as an overlay drawer from
        the right; a tap outside or on a conversation dismisses it. The ☰
        hides while the drawer is open — scrim tap and swipe are the exits.
        Desktop never sees either — the rail is persistent there. %>
    <%= tag.button '☰', aria: { label: 'Conversations' }, data: { 'sidebar-drawer-target': 'toggle', action: 'sidebar-drawer#toggle' },
          class: class_names('sm:hidden fixed right-3 top-3 z-30 cursor-pointer bg-press-dark px-2 py-1 font-mono text-sm leading-none text-kiosk', 'hidden': gated) %>
    <div class="c-shell relative flex w-full flex-col">
      <header class="c-mast-band">
        <%= link_to root_path, class: 'c-poster' do %>
          <span>Comrade</span>
          <svg class="c-poster-star" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="#ffffff" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 17.27L18.18 21l-1.64-7.03L22 9.24l-7.19-.61L12 2 9.19 8.63 2 9.24l5.46 4.73L5.82 21z" /></svg>
        <% end %>
        <%# The reserved title row's heir: a fresh chat reads the date and
            edition; a show page reads the conversation's working title —
            the stream reader fills it there (fresh pages only). %>
        <span id="edition-band" class="c-edition-band"><%= content_for?(:edition) ? yield(:edition) : "#{ Date.current.strftime('%a %b %-d') } · #{ edition_word }" %></span>
      </header>
      <div class="c-mast-sub">
        <p class="c-tagline">Seize the means of information retrieval.</p>
        <nav class="ml-auto flex items-baseline gap-3 overflow-hidden" aria-label="Editions">
          <%= yield :editions %>
          <div class="c-ed-right">
            <%= link_to '+ new', root_path, title: 'New conversation', class: 'c-ed-link' %>
            <%= link_to 'all', all_conversations_path, class: 'c-ed-link' %>
            <% if Conversation.archived.for_enlistee(current_enlistee).exists? %>
              <%= link_to 'archived', archived_conversations_path, class: 'c-ed-link' %>
            <% end %>
          </div>
        </nav>
      </div>
      <div class="flex min-h-0 flex-1">
        <%# The backdrop lives inside the shell: iOS Safari gives position:fixed
            elements their own stacking context, so a body-level backdrop would
            paint over the whole shell — drawer included. Inside, the drawer's
            z-20 outranks it everywhere. %>
        <div data-sidebar-drawer-target="backdrop" class="fixed inset-0 z-10 hidden bg-black/60 sm:hidden"></div>
        <main class="relative flex min-w-0 flex-1 flex-col">
          <%= yield %>
        </main>
        <%= tag.aside class: class_names('c-rail', 'hidden': gated, 'max-sm:fixed max-sm:inset-y-0 max-sm:right-0 max-sm:z-20 max-sm:w-[min(300px,85vw)] max-sm:translate-x-full max-sm:shadow-2xl': true),
              'data-gate-sidebar': true, 'data-sidebar-drawer-target': 'drawer', data: { controller: 'sidebar-edit' } do %>
          <%# Recents carry iOS-style list management: "Edit" flips the list
              into archive mode — rows grow a × control. Archiving removes
              the row in place via Turbo Stream, so edit mode survives
              multi-archive; only archiving the conversation you're viewing
              falls back to a redirect (and there is no minus for it at all). %>
          <div class="mb-2 flex items-baseline justify-between">
            <span class="c-rail-label mb-0">Recent</span>
            <button type="button" data-sidebar-edit-target="toggle" data-action="sidebar-edit#toggle" class="c-rail-link cursor-pointer">Edit</button>
          </div>
          <nav class="-mx-[0.8125rem] min-h-0 flex-1 overflow-y-auto" aria-label="Recent conversations">
            <% Conversation.live.for_enlistee(current_enlistee).order(id: :desc).limit(20).each_with_index do |conversation, index| %>
              <%= tag.div id: dom_id(conversation), class: 'flex items-start' do %>
                <%= link_to conversation_path(conversation), data: { action: 'sidebar-drawer#navigate' },
                      class: class_names('c-idx min-w-0 grow', 'on': request.path == conversation_path(conversation)) do %>
                  <span class="c-idx-num"><%= format('%02d', index + 1) %></span>
                  <span class="c-idx-title"><%= conversation.title.presence || '(Untitled)' %></span>
                  <span class="c-idx-meta"><%= conversation.created_at.strftime('%a') %> · <%= conversation.messages.count %> turns</span>
                <% end %>
                <%# No × for the conversation you're in: archiving it would
                    yank the page out from under you. Leave first, then archive. %>
                <% if request.path != conversation_path(conversation) %>
                  <%= link_to '×', archive_conversation_path(conversation), title: 'Archive',
                        data: { turbo_method: :patch, sidebar_edit_target: 'archive' },
                        class: 'hidden shrink-0 cursor-pointer px-1 pt-1 font-mono text-[0.594rem] text-kiosk hover:text-red-text' %>
                <% end %>
              <% end %>
            <% end %>
          </nav>
          <%# Identity closes the rail: who you are, how comrade talks to
              you, and the text size — the personal cluster, pinned down. %>
          <div class="c-rail-foot">
            <%= render 'layouts/identity', identity_changed: @identity_changed %>
            <%# The font sizer anchors the rail's foot. Its buttons are mono
                links: chrome, not content — root-font scaling must never
                move a click target out from under the cursor. %>
            <span data-controller="font-sizer" class="c-rail-links">
              <button data-action="font-sizer#smaller" aria-label="Smaller text" class="c-rail-link cursor-pointer">A−</button>
              <button data-action="font-sizer#larger" aria-label="Larger text" class="c-rail-link cursor-pointer">A+</button>
            </span>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>
    <%# The focus-debug observer was removed with the iPad autofocus
        hunt's close (2026-11-14): the failure is Firefox for iOS
        failing to activate load-time autofocus — see
        .agent-notes/handoff-rsl-image-attachments.md. %>
    <%# The visual-viewport readout, only under ?vvdebug=1: live
        vv.height/offsetTop, innerHeight, scrollY, and the shell height
        — the numbers the shell's sizing depends on. Auto-nonced. %>
    <% if params[:vvdebug] %>
      <%= javascript_include_tag "vvdebug" %>
    <% end %>
  </body>
</html>
